\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The hardware, attempting to minimize latency, speculatively fills the request with the most recent residue remaining in the L1D Fill Buffer.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The vptestmq instruction transforms this speculative 512-bit residue into a k-mask, which is then leaked via an Oracle Probe (Cache-timing) before the architectural rollback occurs.\
